Kevin Wayne wrote:
> I'm interested in tips by people who eschew Elbereth. I don't
> generally use it much, but there are plenty of times it has gotten me
> out of serious scrapes. I'm just wondering what kinds of tactics I can
> use (besides "Don't get into serious scrapes") other than scribbling
> Elbereth.

Well, a general replacement would be a scroll of scare monster, since it 
works in the same way, basically. Not getting into serious scrapes also 
works, of course...

> Some of the situations I'm thinking of might include
> - the point where you start seeing soldier ants and don't have really
> good armor yet

Go back and get good armor. I think this is the toughest one, actually. 
If you don't want to use Elbereth here, I think the best bet is to use 
escape items to get out, and go up and find better armor.

> - the entrance to the treasure zoo in Sokoban, especially if you don't
> have a tough pet

Just fight them one at a time in the hallway. It has never been a 
problem for me. If it's free, you can even close the door occasionally 
for a breather, but more often than not it becomes blocked.

> - falling through traps or otherwise becoming surrounded by beasties
> and being unable to retreat to a hallway

Use other escape items. Scrolls of teleport, wands of teleport (break 
them in a real emergency) or wands of digging come to mind. Or just try 
to survive by healing, and hit a hole in the group of beasties to 
retreat through. It helps here if you are fast or very fast, otherwise 
you can't easily get away.

